us="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUKI YASUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUKI, YASUO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A process for forming silicon oxide films useful as electrical insulating, dielectric or protective films for LSI, thin film transistors, photoelectric conversion devices, photoreceptors and so on, which comprises forming a coating film made of a polysilane compound represented by the general formula: SinRm(wherein n is an integer of 3 or above; m is an integer of n to 2n+2; and Rs are each independently hydrogen or alkyl) and oxidizing this coating film into a silicon oxide film.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur un procédé de formation de films d'oxyde de silicium servant d'isolants électriques, de diélectriques, ou de films protecteurs des circuits LSI, des transistors à couche mince, des dispositifs de conversion photoélectrique, des photorécepteurs etc. consistant: à former un film d'un composé de polysilane de formule générale SinRm (où n est un entier de 3 ou plus, m est un entier de n à 2n+2, et où les R sont chacun indépendamment H ou alkyle), puis à oxyder le susdit film pour obtenir un film d'oxyde de silicium.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>